From 7044d03e644bf4c1a7f32c2389fcefa5d7fc5ea7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:10:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Admin: stop delete_records() dropping a borrowed reference

Admin_delete_records() takes topic_partition_offsets straight out of
PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords("OO|ff", ...), which hands back a borrowed
reference, and never Py_INCREFs it -- but both the success path and the
err: path end with Py_XDECREF(topic_partition_offsets).  Every call
therefore drops one reference the function does not own.

It is the only such decref in Admin.c: the other functions that decref a
parsed-in object only do so for `future`, which they explicitly
Py_INCREF first because options_to_c() hands it to the background event
callback as the opaque.

Observable without a broker, on any platform and any CPython:

    lst = [TopicPartition("topic", 0, 10)]
    keep = lst
    sys.getrefcount(lst)                  # 3
    admin.delete_records(lst, ...)
    sys.getrefcount(lst)                  # 2

With the usual call style the list is a temporary owned only by the
argument tuple, so the extra decref frees it while the tuple still
references it and the interpreter segfaults later, at an unrelated
point.  tests/test_Admin.py::test_uninitialized_admin_client_methods
reaches it through the err: path and reliably crashes the process --
alone it faults during interpreter shutdown ("Fatal Python error:
Segmentation fault ... <no Python frame>"), and inside a full pytest run
it faults in whatever test happens to run next.

Drop the two decrefs; nothing else in the function touches that
reference.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted yet: confluentinc requires a signed CLA before a pull request can be accepted]
---
 src/confluent_kafka/src/Admin.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/confluent_kafka/src/Admin.c b/src/confluent_kafka/src/Admin.c
index 0c8a970..10e76df 100644
--- a/src/confluent_kafka/src/Admin.c
+++ b/src/confluent_kafka/src/Admin.c
@@ -3272,7 +3272,6 @@ PyObject *Admin_delete_records(Handle *self, PyObject *args, PyObject *kwargs) {
         free(c_obj);
 
         rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_destroy(c_topic_partition_offsets);
-        Py_XDECREF(topic_partition_offsets);
 
         Py_RETURN_NONE;
 err:
@@ -3288,7 +3287,6 @@ err:
                 rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_destroy(
                     c_topic_partition_offsets);
         }
-        Py_XDECREF(topic_partition_offsets);
         return NULL;
 }
 
